// A hexadecimal prefix is `0x` in lower case only. At `0XFF` the longest match
// is the NUMBER `0`, and `XFF` is a name, so the program has a name directly
// after a literal, a syntax error (spec/01-lexical.md, row `suffix-boundary`).
// A scanner that reads `0X` as a prefix, as C, Java, and Python do, accepts it.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line
// prints `ran`, so an implementation that finds the error only when it runs
// the program prints `ran` and fails this probe.

print "ran";
print 0XFF;

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal suffix-boundary
